  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ebola sensitisation and orphan mapping -contribution to December 2014 &apos;Western Surge&apos; in Freetown</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of 14 December, the cumulative number of confirmed, probable and suspected cases of Ebola Virus Disease (EVD) in Sierra Leone is estimated to have reached 8,356, with a total of 2,085 deaths. The number of cases has surprised those in Liberia, leaving Sierra Leone the worst affected country. 

The Western Area of Sierra Leone, where the capital Freetown is located, is one of the areas worst affected by the outbreak and where transmission remains persistent. The Government and aid agencies have introduced stiff measures to try and stem the spread of the disease. The 15 day &quot;Western Area Surge&quot; exercise includes travel restrictions and additional sensitisation programmes. 

This 15 day StreetChild project is a contribution to the &apos;Western Area Surge&quot; over the Christmas period and will provide ebola education to 20,250 families, strengthen community structures to identify and report ebola cases and record ebola orphans or any children who are vulnerable as a result of the outbreak.</narrative>
  </description>
